# Recipe Platform — Cursor Rules
# Stack: Next.js 14 (App Router) · Supabase · Tailwind CSS · TypeScript

---

## General Principles

- Always use TypeScript. Never use `any` — use proper types or `unknown`.
- Prefer Server Components by default. Only use `'use client'` when necessary (event handlers, hooks, browser APIs).
- Follow Next.js 14 App Router conventions strictly (layouts, loading, error, page files).
- Keep components small and focused. If a component exceeds ~150 lines, split it up.
- Never hardcode secrets or API keys. Always use environment variables from `.env.local`.
- Always handle loading and error states explicitly.

---

## Project Structure

Follow this structure exactly:

```
/app
  /layout.tsx
  /page.tsx
  /auth/login/page.tsx
  /auth/signup/page.tsx
  /recipes/page.tsx
  /recipes/[id]/page.tsx
  /recipes/new/page.tsx
  /recipes/[id]/edit/page.tsx
  /profile/[username]/page.tsx
  /profile/me/page.tsx
/components
  /ui/          # Generic reusable UI (Button, Input, Card, Badge, etc.)
  /recipes/     # RecipeCard, RecipeForm, IngredientList, StepList, etc.
  /layout/      # Navbar, Footer, SearchBar
  /auth/        # LoginForm, SignupForm
/lib
  /supabase/
    client.ts   # Browser Supabase client
    server.ts   # Server Supabase client
  /actions/     # Next.js Server Actions
  /validations/ # Zod schemas
/types
  database.ts   # Supabase generated types
```

---

## TypeScript

- Import Supabase database types from `@/types/database.ts`.
- Define component prop types inline with `interface` for clarity.
- Use `Database['public']['Tables']['recipes']['Row']` pattern for table row types.
- Always type Server Action return values explicitly.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
interface RecipeCardProps {
  recipe: Database['public']['Tables']['recipes']['Row'] & {
    profiles: Pick<Profile, 'username' | 'display_name' | 'avatar_url'>
  }
}

// ❌ Bad
function RecipeCard({ recipe }: { recipe: any }) {}
```

---

## Supabase

- Use the **server client** (`@/lib/supabase/server.ts`) in Server Components and Server Actions.
- Use the **browser client** (`@/lib/supabase/client.ts`) only in Client Components.
- Always check for errors after every Supabase call.
- Never expose the service role key to the client.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — server component
const supabase = createClient()
const { data, error } = await supabase.from('recipes').select('*')
if (error) throw new Error(error.message)

// ❌ Bad — ignoring errors
const { data } = await supabase.from('recipes').select('*')
```

- Always use `.single()` when fetching by ID and handle the case where data is null.
- Use Supabase Storage for all image uploads. Never store base64 images in the database.
- Always scope storage paths by user ID: `recipe-images/{userId}/{filename}`.

---

## Server Actions

- All mutations (create, update, delete) must be Server Actions in `/lib/actions/`.
- Always validate input with Zod before touching the database.
- Always verify the user session at the top of every Server Action.
- Return a typed result object, never throw raw errors to the client.

```typescript
// ✅ Good pattern for Server Actions
'use server'

import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'
import { recipeSchema } from '@/lib/validations/recipe'

export async function createRecipe(formData: FormData) {
  const supabase = createClient()
  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  if (!user) return { error: 'Unauthorized' }

  const parsed = recipeSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(formData))
  if (!parsed.success) return { error: parsed.error.flatten() }

  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('recipes')
    .insert({ ...parsed.data, user_id: user.id })
    .select()
    .single()

  if (error) return { error: error.message }
  return { data }
}
```

---

## Components & React

- Use `async/await` in Server Components for data fetching — no `useEffect` for data fetching.
- Only use `'use client'` for: forms, interactive UI (likes, saves), modals, toast notifications.
- Use React Hook Form + Zod for all forms. Never use uncontrolled raw form elements.
- Use `useTransition` for optimistic UI updates on likes/saves.
- Never fetch data inside Client Components if it can be done in a Server Component and passed as props.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — fetch in Server Component, pass as props
// app/recipes/[id]/page.tsx (Server Component)
const { data: recipe } = await supabase.from('recipes').select('*').eq('id', id).single()
return <RecipeDetail recipe={recipe} />

// ❌ Bad — fetching in Client Component unnecessarily
'use client'
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/recipes/' + id).then(...)
}, [])
```

---

## Tailwind CSS

- Use Tailwind utility classes only. No inline styles, no CSS modules, no external CSS unless absolutely necessary.
- Use `clsx` or `cn()` (from `tailwind-merge`) for conditional class names.
- Mobile-first responsive design. Start with base styles, layer up with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`.
- Use a consistent spacing scale. Stick to `4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64px` (Tailwind's `1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16`).
- Extract repeated class combinations into reusable components, not into `@apply`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'
<button className={cn('px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-medium', isActive && 'bg-orange-500 text-white')} />

// ❌ Bad
<button style={{ padding: '8px 16px' }} className={isActive ? 'active' : ''} />
```

---

## Authentication & Authorization

- Always use `supabase.auth.getUser()` (not `getSession()`) on the server for security.
- Protect routes via `middleware.ts` — never rely solely on UI hiding.
- Always check `user.id === resource.user_id` before allowing edits or deletes.
- Never trust client-sent `user_id` values — always derive from the server session.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — derive user_id from session in Server Action
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
if (!user) return { error: 'Unauthorized' }
// use user.id, don't accept it from the form

// ❌ Bad
const userId = formData.get('user_id') // never trust this
```

---

## Row Level Security (RLS)

- RLS must be enabled on every table. Never disable it.
- All queries must work correctly with RLS enabled — never use the service role key to bypass RLS in normal app flows.
- When adding a new table, always write and test RLS policies before using the table in the app.

---

## Forms & Validation

- Define all Zod schemas in `/lib/validations/`.
- Share the same schema between client-side validation and server-side Server Action validation.
- Use descriptive error messages in Zod schemas that can be shown directly to users.

```typescript
// /lib/validations/recipe.ts
import { z } from 'zod'

export const recipeSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(3, 'Title must be at least 3 characters').max(100),
  description: z.string().max(500).optional(),
  prep_time: z.coerce.number().min(0).max(1440),
  cook_time: z.coerce.number().min(0).max(1440),
  servings: z.coerce.number().min(1).max(100),
  difficulty: z.enum(['easy', 'medium', 'hard']),
  cuisine: z.string().max(50).optional(),
})
```

---

## Image Uploads

- Always validate file type and size before uploading (max 5MB, jpg/png/webp only).
- Generate unique filenames using `crypto.randomUUID()` to avoid collisions.
- Store only the public URL in the database, not the storage path.
- Use Next.js `<Image>` component for all images — never raw `<img>` tags.
- Add Supabase Storage domain to `next.config.js` `images.remotePatterns`.

```typescript
// next.config.js
images: {
  remotePatterns: [
    {
      protocol: 'https',
      hostname: '*.supabase.co',
      pathname: '/storage/v1/object/public/**',
    },
  ],
},
```

---

## Error Handling

- Every page must have an `error.tsx` sibling file.
- Every async route segment must have a `loading.tsx` with a skeleton UI.
- Never show raw Supabase or database error messages to the user — log them server-side and show a friendly message.
- Use toast notifications (e.g. `react-hot-toast` or `sonner`) for mutation feedback.

---

## Performance

- Use Next.js `<Image>` with explicit `width` and `height` or `fill` for all images.
- Paginate all list queries — never fetch unbounded lists. Default page size: 12.
- Use `Suspense` boundaries around async Server Components for streaming.
- Memoize expensive Client Component computations with `useMemo`.

---

## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase | `RecipeCard.tsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useRecipeLike.ts` |
| Server Actions | camelCase verb phrases | `createRecipe`, `deleteComment` |
| Database tables | snake_case plural | `recipes`, `saved_recipes` |
| Environment variables | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE | `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` |
| Zod schemas | camelCase with `Schema` suffix | `recipeSchema` |
| TypeScript types/interfaces | PascalCase | `Recipe`, `UserProfile` |

---

## What NOT to Do

- Do not use the Pages Router (`/pages` directory). App Router only.
- Do not use `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps`.
- Do not use `useEffect` for data fetching.
- Do not store sensitive data (passwords, tokens) in localStorage.
- Do not use `any` in TypeScript.
- Do not bypass RLS with the service role key in client-facing code.
- Do not commit `.env.local` to version control.
- Do not use raw `<img>` tags — always use Next.js `<Image>`.
- Do not write mutations directly in components — always use Server Actions.
- Do not use `router.push` after a Server Action for revalidation — use `revalidatePath` instead.
